        {
          "id": "note",
          "kind": "note",
          "data": {
            "text": "## Satellite pass\n\n**GPS position** is your station. Everything that points or predicts needs it.\n\n**Satellite** predicts the next pass and, during it, drives two things at once: the decoder's tuning for Doppler, and the rotator's aim.\n\n**Rotator** points the antenna. Without one, delete it: the rest still works on a fixed antenna.\n\n**Channel** decodes APT. Pick the satellite in the Satellite node, not here.\n\n**Video** is where the weather image appears, line by line as the pass comes in. APT sends a picture, so without this node the pass decodes to a log of rows you cannot look at.\n\n**Recorder** keeps the raw IQ of the pass, so you can decode it again later with different settings.\n\n**Map** draws the ground track. **Decoder log** keeps what came down.\n\nPick a radio on the Device node to start."
          },
